// tsconfig.fixtures.json — the FIXTURE-CORPUS typecheck target (31-06, closing gap 2).
//
// WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. `scripts/runnable-ref/fixtures/**` was excluded from BOTH other targets, so
// `union-all-arms.uat.spec.ts` could import `describe` from `@playwright/test` — a binding that
// package does not export — and no command in this repository ever said so. The fixture meant to
// prove D-14 arm (c) was not representative of real Playwright code, which is precisely why the
// shipped 47-of-47 green suite could not have caught arm (c) matching a spelling Playwright never
// produces. A corpus outside the reach of a typecheck is not evidence.
//
// WHY A THIRD TARGET RATHER THAN LOOSENING EITHER OF THE OTHER TWO.
//   - `tsconfig.json` is the SHIPPED-SOURCE target. Its exclude list must stay byte-unchanged so
//     `npm run build` and `npm run freshness` keep emitting exactly the same committed `.js` set.
//     Pulling the fixtures in there would emit a `.js` twin for every corpus file and the freshness
//     gate would then demand those twins be committed.
//   - `tsconfig.tests.json` exists to give the dead-code flags REACH over `**/*.test.ts`. The
//     fixtures are a parse corpus, not tooling source; they belong to their own target, which can
//     point at a declared `@playwright/test` surface without that declaration leaking into the
//     target that checks the tooling.
//
// WHAT IT CHECKS AGAINST. `scripts/runnable-ref/fixtures/playwright-test.d.ts`, a hand-transcribed
// declaration of the surface this corpus uses. Read that file's header before trusting it: its
// drift from the upstream package is an open `UNKNOWN - verify`.
//
// 31-34 (D-35): it ALSO checks against `scripts/runnable-ref/fixtures/foreign-framework.d.ts`, the
// ambient surface of two modules that are NOT `@playwright/test`. CR-23's corpus rows drive a
// `describe.skip` group and an `expect.soft` assertion whose bindings come from those modules, which
// is the spelling the retained ban heads exist for. Those declarations are a SHAPE, not a
// transcription of any shipped library — read that file's header before reading them as anything
// else.
//
// This target sets `noEmit` and emits nothing at all. It is wired into `npm run typecheck`, so a
// fixture regression fails the same command CI and every plan's verify step already run.
{
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "noEmit": true
  },
  "include": [
    "scripts/runnable-ref/fixtures/**/*.uat.spec.ts",
    "scripts/runnable-ref/fixtures/playwright-test.d.ts",
    "scripts/runnable-ref/fixtures/foreign-framework.d.ts"
  ],
  "exclude": ["node_modules", ".tmp-build"]
}
